Resumen

Introduced for the media/promotions feature: the newly added CRUD endpoints rely on the existing global role check plus any-membership tenant check instead of verifying that the caller has admin or owner role for the specific tenant in the URL.

The new media and promotion endpoints are registered on tenant_admin_router, whose admin check is based only on request.state.roles from the JWT. Those roles are not tied to the {tenant_id} path parameter. The later tenant access check allows access to a different path tenant if has_user_tenant_role finds any role for that tenant, without requiring admin/owner for that tenant. As a result, a user who is admin in tenant A and merely viewer/agent/member in tenant B can call /tenants/{tenant_b}/media and /tenants/{tenant_b}/promotions, after which the handlers explicitly set app.tenant_id to tenant B and perform reads/writes/deletes. This lets a lower-privileged tenant member list media metadata, upload/delete media assets, and create/update/delete promotions that the bot may send to tenant B's customers.

Validación

 Confirm new media/promotions endpoints are mounted on tenant_admin_router and inherit only the global require_min_role('admin') router dependency.
 Confirm authentication stores roles in request.state.roles without binding those roles to the {tenant_id} path parameter.
 Confirm ensure_tenant_access accepts a database membership row for the path tenant and has_user_tenant_role does not require admin/owner role for that tenant.
 Confirm affected handlers set app.tenant_id to the path tenant and then read or mutate tenant-scoped media/promotion data.
 Dynamically reproduce with controls: tenant A admin + victim tenant membership succeeds, no victim membership fails, and no global admin fails.
